- the inverse morphism sends `x` to `x⁻¹`;
- the multiplication morphism sends `(a,b)` to `a * b`;
- the unit morphism from the singleton tensor unit is constantly `1`;
- the underlying type of the reconstructed internal group is `CommGrpCat.carrier A`.

Thus each of the four universally quantified propositions is true independently, essentially by definitional reduction plus the standard simp lemmas for this equivalence and concrete morphism evaluation. Prove these four pointwise facts first, after changing tensor elements to pairs and tensor-unit elements to the singleton type. Then construct each `Iff` by ignoring its hypothesis and returning the corresponding already-established fact, and combine the two equivalences with `And.intro`. The main technical issue is only exposing the definitions hidden by the fully elaborated categorical expressions; no substantive algebraic argument is needed.

